+    "field": "content_html",
+    "find": "<p data-narration-id=\"n14\">When commenting on outliers in exam questions, you should: (1) identify the outlier by referring to its approximate value, (2) suggest whether it might be a genuine extreme value or a possible error, and (3) comment on its effect on any averages you have calculated. An outlier pulls the mean towards it but does not affect the median.</p>",
+    "replace": "<p data-narration-id=\"n14\">When commenting on outliers in exam questions, you should: (1) identify the outlier by referring to its approximate value, (2) suggest whether it might be a genuine extreme value or a possible error, and (3) comment on its effect on any averages you have calculated. An outlier can pull the mean towards it. The median is usually less affected.</p>",
+    "severity": "HIGH",
